title: edit silently retypes an encrypted non-finite float to a string
updated: 2026-08-21T07:10:07Z
---

Found while measuring karr #123 (sops 3.13.3 at /tmp/sops). NOT the same
defect and NOT fixed by karr #123 -- it is the ENCRYPTED-slot half of the same
plaintext round trip, it is SILENT, and it is therefore worse.

MEASURED, one document, key `keep` in an encrypted slot:

  printf 'keep: .inf\nother: x\n' | sops -e   ->  keep: ENC[...,type:float]
                                       sops -d   ->  keep: .inf

  File::SOPS->edit on that file, editor changes `other` only:
      returns 1, no warning, sops -d exit 0
      wire AFTER: keep: ENC[...,type:str]
      sops -d    : keep: Inf          <- a STRING now, not a number

  sops edit on the same file, same editor:
      exit 0, wire unchanged: type:float, sops -d prints `keep: .inf`

MECHANISM. The encrypted leaf decrypts to a real Perl infinity. The plaintext
emitter (Format::YAML::emit -> YAML::XS::Dump) writes a bare non-finite NV as
`Inf` / `-Inf` / `NaN` -- tokens go-yaml resolves as STRINGS (they are the near
misses ADR 0026 measured, and correctly leaves alone). So the editor is shown
`Inf`, the string `Inf` comes back, detect_type says str, and the leaf is
re-encrypted as type:str. karr #123 cannot reach this: its repair keys on the
twelve %GO_CONSTANT tokens, and `Inf` is not one of them -- correctly, because
a user who types `Inf` really does mean the string.

The same emitter defect makes decrypt_file diverge from `sops -d` for the same
document: we write `keep: Inf`, sops writes `keep: .inf`. And decrypt_file ->
encrypt_file therefore retypes the leaf as well, silently, with no editor
involved.

WHERE THE FIX HAS TO GO. At the emit, not the parse -- the plaintext has
genuinely destroyed the information by the time it is reparsed. A bare
non-finite NV in a document with no MAC should be written as its go-yaml token
(`.inf`, `-.inf`, `.nan`), which is what sops -d writes and what ADR 0026
already established as the right carrier. It cannot go in Format::YAML alone:
Encrypted::_canonical_floats short-circuits a non-finite leaf with
`return $node unless _carries_go_non_finite_token(...)` before any handler hook
is reached, so the leaf never sees `carrier`. Doing it in the handler would
mean a second full tree walk in emit AND a second copy of the NO_AGREED_FORM
decision -- this distribution's signature defect.

So it needs lib/File/SOPS/Encrypted.pm, which was outside karr #123's
boundary (karr #122/#114 were in flight there). Wire lane.

Note the interaction with karr #122: once encrypt_value can see the format, a
YAML encrypted slot can carry type:float/+Inf again, and then this round trip
closes properly in both directions.
2026-08-21 07:07 Fixed at the emit, in lib/File/SOPS/Encrypted.pm. ADR 0037.

THE TICKET'S CENTRAL CLAIM WAS VERIFIED FIRST and holds: a canonical_float_tree
call with three recording callbacks shows that for +Inf/-Inf/NaN NONE of
roundtrips, carrier or reject_scalar is invoked -- the leaf leaves the walk
unchanged. No fix in a format handler could have reached it.

EXTENT, wider than the ticket said. decrypt_file diverges exactly as filed
(0 of 3 leaf lines matched sops -d, now 3 of 3). JSON is NOT the same defect
but a worse one: decrypt_file wrote "secret": null, and edit replaced the whole
ENC[...] with a bare UNENCRYPTED null -- the value destroyed, not retyped --
where sops refuses the same document (sops -d --output-type json and sops edit
both exit 4).

TARGET FORM, measured: sops -d writes .inf / -.inf / .nan for an encrypted
type:float, in both wire formats. For JSON there is no reference form to copy,
so the answer given is sops's own: refuse, naming the key path.

MECHANISM: the walk asks the handler's own carrier for the token and verifies
the answer with ADR 0031's gate (public token bytes AND value_to_bytes must
both come back as the same bytes). The YAML carrier answers with a dualvar
unchanged; the JSON carrier croaks. No handler file touched. Fails closed both
directions. Only a leaf with NO public PV is repaired, so ADR 0031's banana row
and the three contradictions are untouched in both directions -- measured.

CIRCLE CLOSES: emit .inf -> ADR 0026 parse (ungated since ADR 0034) -> float,
digest +Inf, token as its text. Verified for all three.

karr #122 IS THE REMAINING RUNG, and edit now croaks there instead of
corrupting. A measured note is on that ticket: its premise (the two formats
disagree) is wrong -- both WIRE formats behave identically, only the OUTPUT
format differs.

